<section class="band" id="faq"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head"><h2>Good to know</h2></div>
  <div class="faq">
    <details open><summary>What is Wild Willows?</summary><p>A cozy nature-restoration life sim. You set up camp at the edge of a damaged nature preserve, then gather materials, craft and plant real habitat, and shape the land. As each biome recovers, real animal species find their way home.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is Wild Willows free?</summary><p>There's a free demo you can play right in your browser on the itch.io page. The full game is a one-time purchase on the Mac App Store and on itch.io. No ads, no in-app purchases, no loot boxes.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What platforms is it on?</summary><p>The full game is on the Mac App Store for macOS, and on itch.io for macOS, Windows, and Linux. A free browser demo lives on the itch.io page too.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What languages does it support?</summary><p>English and Spanish. You can switch language on the title screen or in Settings at any time.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does it have accessibility options?</summary><p>Yes: a reduce-motion setting, colorblind palettes (red-green, blue-yellow, and high-contrast monochrome), a choice of five interface fonts, adjustable text size, and a plain-language option.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is there any combat or a way to lose?</summary><p>No. There's no combat, no enemies, and no way to fail. Animals are observed and welcomed home, never hunted, captured, or lost, and nothing ever dies.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I use Wild Willows in a classroom?</summary><p>Yes, and there\u2019s a kit for it: a free educator guide and six student worksheets, both up in <a href="#educators">For teachers</a>. The lesson runs in one 45&ndash;60 minute period for grades 5&ndash;8 and works with the free demo. If cost is what\u2019s standing in the way, I keep a limited number of free promo codes for classrooms. Tell me a bit about why you want to use it with your class and write to <a href="mailto:wildwillowsgame@gmail.com">wildwillowsgame@gmail.com</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is it family-friendly?</summary><p>Yes. It's gentle, non-violent and educational, and rated 9+ on the App Store.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I need an internet connection?</summary><p>No. The game is fully playable offline, with no account and no sign-in. Your world lives on your own device.</p></details>
  </div>
</div></section>

